(6492732, 964061, 39057, '<td valign="top">Edit: Sorry about the title remark...I should have looked it up! I gave the same score though<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kenskid:</b></div><hr/><i> Should be on the front along with the other one like it. I think you may lose a few tenths overall because your title doesn''t seem to go with one of the senses. However, I think it screams sense of "sight" as well as touch (the barbs).<br/> <br/>Good luck. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Edit: Sorry about the title remark...I should have looked it up! I gave the same score though Originally posted by kenskid: Should be on the front along with the other one like it. I think you may lose a few tenths overall because your title doesn''t seem to go with one of the senses. However, I think it screams sense of "sight" as well as touch (the barbs). Good luck. ', '2011-08-04 11:51:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(6493237, 963902, 104499, '<td valign="top">This photo is just not that good. Foot is dead center in the composition. The theme of the photo is tickle me, ok so if<br/>you don''t have a foot fetish the photo is pointless. Looks like a average backyard  vacation snap, nothing more.</td>', 'This photo is just not that good. Foot is dead center in the composition. The theme of the photo is tickle me, ok so ifyou don''t have a foot fetish the photo is pointless. Looks like a average backyard  vacation snap, nothing more.', '2011-08-04 17:15:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(6493759, 963836, 74559, '<td valign="top">Wow, what a fine lighting capture, and it basic editing! You chose a great location to take the image; the silhouetted foreground is wonderful in its variety of vegetation from, ummm, bushy thingies to poky thingies to a saguaro :-) It must have been quite an active storm to catch this much activity in a 19 second exposure, what a treat!</td>', 'Wow, what a fine lighting capture, and it basic editing! You chose a great location to take the image; the silhouetted foreground is wonderful in its variety of vegetation from, ummm, bushy thingies to poky thingies to a saguaro :-) It must have been quite an active storm to catch this much activity in a 19 second exposure, what a treat!', '2011-08-05 01:27:06.000000', NULL, 0),
